                <pb facs="0976" n="862" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg862"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.632/104: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Austria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stockton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-02T13:00:00+01:00">April 2, 1931—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>26. Department’s 15, April 1, 1 p.m. Foreign Office has just informed me
                    officially Austrian President ratified supplemental article and <pb facs="0977"
                        n="863" xml:id="pg863"/> reservation March 28th. Necessary countersignatures
                    of Chancellor, Minister for Foreign Affairs, and Minister of Commerce have since
                    been affixed and Austria is now ready to effect exchange. Urge President’s
                    ratification be expedited.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
